Revert of the reload() hunk of FSF GCC r13805 (gcc-mirror/gcc commit
2a9fb5489fc58447f5a69fa7a607d08dd263ac4a), applied to the
cygnus-2.7.2-970404 source (decompals/old-gcc b18.tar.gz).

Original commit: Ian Lance Taylor, Wed Mar 26 1997,
"Add a CSE pass over the hard registers after reload is complete".
ChangeLog.fsf entry in the 970404 tree:

  Wed Mar 26 12:34:21 1997  Ian Lance Taylor  <ian@cygnus.com>

	* reload1.c (reload): Call reload_cse_regs.
	(reg_values): New static variable.
	(reload_cse_invalidate_regno): New static function.
	...

This patch is exactly the reverse of the commit's "(reload): Call
reload_cse_regs" hunk.  The other hunks only add static functions, which
the 970404 tree has already revised (reload_cse_noop_set_p takes two
arguments there), so they are left in place and become unused.  The Sony
safechk 2.0.0.x module (notes/overlays/apv2.md) was compiled before this
change: with it, `move rX,zero` delay-loop addresses become copies of
another register holding zero.

--- a/reload1.c
+++ b/reload1.c
@@ -2135,10 +2135,6 @@
 	}
     }
 
-  /* Do a very simple CSE pass over just the hard registers.  */
-  if (optimize > 0)
-    reload_cse_regs (first);
-
 #ifdef PRESERVE_DEATH_INFO_REGNO_P
